hifiberry-audiocontrol (0.8.8) trixie; urgency=medium

  Player definitions have moved out of /etc/audiocontrol/audiocontrol.json into
  /etc/audiocontrol/players.d/, one file per package that provides a player.
  The players array is removed from an existing audiocontrol.json on upgrade; a
  copy of the previous file is left as audiocontrol.json.bak.

  Three consequences:

  * A player you disabled with "enable": false in audiocontrol.json becomes
    enabled again, because that entry is removed and the package default
    applies. Re-apply the setting in the matching file under
    /etc/audiocontrol/players.d/. This is most visible for librespot, which
    reappears as a Spotify Connect endpoint on the network.

  * The files under /etc/audiocontrol/players.d/ for librespot, shairport and
    squeezelite were previously generated by each of those packages' own
    postinst scripts, not hand-written. Upgrading those packages will
    therefore show a conffile prompt for librespot.json, shairport.json and
    squeezelite.json on essentially every device that has them installed, not
    just ones with local edits. This is expected; accept the packaged version
    unless you deliberately changed it.

  * If a player was in use without its matching HiFiBerry package installed -
    for example a "bluetooth" entry running against stock Debian bluez, or an
    "mpd" entry talking to Debian's own mpd rather than hifiberry-mpd - its
    definition is removed from audiocontrol.json and nothing replaces it,
    since no HiFiBerry package is present to install the include. Re-create it
    by hand as a file under /etc/audiocontrol/players.d/; the previous
    definition is preserved in audiocontrol.json.bak to copy from.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 13:24:53 +0000
